On 5/24/07, Vid Sintef <picos.picos@gmail.com> wrote:
> By the way, did you use {xy} because the language of it's content is {xelso}?
> And, in another case, {gy} for {glico}? If so, I didn't know that! Cool!

Some people do that, yes (that is, use {gy} specifically because what
they are quoting is in English).

It's not required, though -- "Lojban" doesn't care what you use.

Others like to use {zoi} as the delimiter, as in {zoi .zoi. This is
the delimiter .zoi.}. The important thing is really only that the
delimiter not appear in the text you are quoting.


